# Ask Me Why, initial verse "I love you ..." (figure 33.1)
# Thirteen bars in three phrases, led in by E7 f#7 on beats 3 and 4. Pollack types a beat row
# ("beats: 1, 2, 3, 4") over the bars: the split bars have two chords of two beats each, and the
# "- E7 f#7" bar holds E for two beats with E7 and f#7 on beats 3 and 4, as in the lead-in.
#? Pollack's "E7" (I) and "g#7" sound on the record like E major 7th and g#-minor 7th; E7 is kept as typed but would play as a dominant seventh.
key E

system m. 1
